   "skos:definition": "The Old Testament book that tells how Solomon succeeded David, built the Temple in Jerusalem and then turned to other gods, how the kingdom split into Israel and Judah under Jeroboam and Rehoboam, and how prophets such as Ahijah, Elijah and Micaiah held the kings to account down to the death of Ahab; with 2 Kings it was originally one book, Kings.",
