   "skos:definition": "The twenty-book Greek history of the Jewish people from creation to the eve of the revolt against Rome in AD 66, completed by the Jewish historian Flavius Josephus around AD 93–94; it retells the biblical story for Greco-Roman readers and is the richest outside witness to the world of the New Testament, mentioning John the Baptist, James \"the brother of Jesus\", and (in a disputed passage) Jesus himself.",
