   "skos:broader": {
    "@id": "bg:old-testament"
   },
   "skos:definition": "The poetic writing of the Hebrew Bible (by one estimate about a third of the Bible, including Psalms, Proverbs, Job, Lamentations, the Song of Songs and much of the prophets), built from short paired lines that echo and develop each other, rich imagery and occasional patterns such as alphabetic acrostics.",
