  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/1-kings/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:1-kings"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What does Solomon ask God for at Gibeon in 1 Kings 3:5-9, and what does God give him besides (3:12-13)?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/1-kings/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:1-kings"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In his prayer at the Temple's dedication, Solomon admits that heaven cannot contain God (1 Kings 8:27). Why build a house at all? How does Stephen use the same idea in Acts 7:47-50?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/1-kings/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:1-kings"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Read 1 Kings 8:46-50. Whom does Solomon expect to pray toward the Temple, and from where? How would these verses have sounded to Israelites in exile?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/1-kings/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:1-kings"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to 1 Kings 11:1-13, what turned Solomon's heart, and why is the kingdom not torn away in his own lifetime?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/1-kings/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:1-kings"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Compare the advice Rehoboam rejects and the advice he follows in 1 Kings 12:6-15. What does this chapter teach about power and listening?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/1-kings/check/6",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:1-kings"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Micaiah says he will speak only what the LORD tells him, though four hundred prophets say otherwise (1 Kings 22:6-17). Where is it hard for you to hear, or to say, an unwelcome truth?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:abraham"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What three things does God promise Abram in Genesis 12:1-3, and who, finally, is to be blessed through him?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:abraham"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Genesis 15:6 says Abram believed and it was credited to him as righteousness. What had God just promised him (15:1-5), and what in his circumstances made it hard to believe?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:abraham"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Compare Genesis 12:10-20 and Genesis 16:1-4 with Genesis 22:1-18. What do the earlier stories show about Abraham's fears and shortcuts, and how has his trust grown by chapter 22?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:abraham"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Genesis 18:22-33 Abraham bargains with God over Sodom. What does he appeal to in verse 25, and what does this teach about bold, honest prayer?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:abraham"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Paul (Romans 4) and James (James 2:21-24) both use Abraham. Which episodes does each one point to, and how can both be true at once?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham/check/6",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:abraham"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Hebrews 11:8 says Abraham \"went out, not knowing where he went.\" Where is God asking you to take a next step before you can see the whole road?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abrahamic-covenant/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:abrahamic-covenant"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What three things does God promise Abram in Genesis 12:1-3 and 12:7, and who, in the end, is meant to be blessed?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abrahamic-covenant/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:abrahamic-covenant"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Genesis 15:9-18, who passes between the divided animals, and what does Jeremiah 34:18 suggest that rite meant?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abrahamic-covenant/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:abrahamic-covenant"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What does God add in Genesis 17 (a new name, an \"everlasting covenant\", a sign), and why does Paul stress in Romans 4:9-11 that Abraham was counted righteous before he was circumcised?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abrahamic-covenant/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:abrahamic-covenant"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Galatians 3:17 says the law, coming 430 years later, cannot cancel the promise. What difference does it make that God's promise came first?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abrahamic-covenant/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:abrahamic-covenant"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Hebrews 6:13-18 says God bound himself with an oath so that his people would have \"strong encouragement\". Which of God's promises do you find hardest to rest on, and how might Abraham's story help?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/acts-of-the-apostles/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:acts-of-the-apostles"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Compare Luke 1:1-4 with Acts 1:1-3. Who is addressed in both, and what does Acts say the \"former treatise\" was about?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/acts-of-the-apostles/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:acts-of-the-apostles"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Acts 1:8 names Jerusalem, Judea and Samaria, and \"the uttermost part of the earth.\" Trace where the story is in chapters 2, 8, 10 and 28. How does the book follow that map?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/acts-of-the-apostles/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:acts-of-the-apostles"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What question brought the apostles and elders together in Acts 15:1-6, and how does the phrase \"it seemed good to the Holy Spirit, and to us\" (15:28) describe the way they reached a decision?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/acts-of-the-apostles/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:acts-of-the-apostles"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Acts ends with Paul under guard in Rome yet preaching \"with all boldness, none forbidding him\" (28:31). Why might Luke end there rather than with Paul's trial, and what does that say about the ongoing story the church still lives in?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/antiquities-of-the-jews/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:antiquities-of-the-jews"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Compare Mark 6:17-29 with Josephus's account of John the Baptist. What do they agree on, and what does each writer stress about why Herod Antipas killed John?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/antiquities-of-the-jews/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:antiquities-of-the-jews"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Read Acts 12:20-23 and then the summary of Josephus's account of Agrippa's death. Which details are shared, and what does Luke add about the reason for Herod's death?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/antiquities-of-the-jews/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:antiquities-of-the-jews"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Galatians 1:19 Paul meets \"James, the Lord's brother\". How does Josephus's report of James's death help a reader picture the James of Acts and Galatians?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/antiquities-of-the-jews/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:antiquities-of-the-jews"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Why might it matter to Christians that a Jewish historian who did not follow Jesus nonetheless mentions John, James and Jesus? What are the limits of that kind of evidence?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/babylonian-exile/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:babylonian-exile"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to 2 Kings 24:10-16 and 25:8-12, who was taken to Babylon in each deportation, and who was left behind in the land?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/babylonian-exile/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:babylonian-exile"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What does Jeremiah tell the exiles to do in Jeremiah 29:4-7, and why might that have surprised people who expected to go home soon?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/babylonian-exile/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:babylonian-exile"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Psalm 137 asks how anyone can sing the Lord's song in a foreign land. How do Ezekiel 1:1-3 and Isaiah 40:1-2 answer that question in different ways?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/babylonian-exile/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:babylonian-exile"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Matthew 1:17 divides Jesus's family tree at the exile. What does that tell you about how the first Christians understood where Jesus fits in Israel's story?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/babylonian-exile/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:babylonian-exile"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "1 Peter 1:1 and 1:17 call Christians foreigners and exiles. Where do you feel \"away from home\" in your own life or church, and what would it look like to seek the peace of the place where God has put you?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/barnabas/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:barnabas"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Acts 4:36-37, what was Barnabas's real name, where was he from, and what did he do with his field?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/barnabas/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:barnabas"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Acts 9:26-27, why were the disciples in Jerusalem afraid of Saul, and what did Barnabas tell the apostles about him?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/barnabas/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:barnabas"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What did Barnabas see when he arrived in Antioch (Acts 11:22-24), and how did he respond?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/barnabas/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:barnabas"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Compare the order of the names in Acts 13:2 and 13:7 with Acts 13:46. What change in the mission does it hint at?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/barnabas/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:barnabas"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Barnabas gave Mark a second chance after Mark had left the work (Acts 15:36-39). Who in your church or life might need someone to vouch for them, and what would it cost you to do it?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/biblical-canon/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:biblical-canon"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Luke 24:44, which three groups of writings does the risen Jesus say speak about him?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/biblical-canon/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:biblical-canon"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "How does 2 Peter 3:15-16 describe Paul's letters, and what does that suggest about how early Christians regarded them?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/biblical-canon/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:biblical-canon"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Why might it matter that the canon was recognised gradually by the whole church, rather than chosen in a single meeting?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/biblical-canon/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:biblical-canon"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "If your Bible has fewer or more Old Testament books than a friend's from another tradition, how could you talk about the difference with charity and accuracy?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/binding-of-isaac/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:binding-of-isaac"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Genesis 22:1 tells the reader something Abraham is not told. What is it, and how does knowing it change the way you read the rest of the chapter?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/binding-of-isaac/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:binding-of-isaac"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Isaac asks in Genesis 22:7, \"where is the lamb?\" Compare Abraham's answer in 22:8 with what happens in 22:13-14. What name does Abraham give the place, and why?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/binding-of-isaac/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:binding-of-isaac"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What reasons does the angel give in Genesis 22:12 and 22:16-18 for God's words to Abraham? What does God promise, and for whose sake?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/binding-of-isaac/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:binding-of-isaac"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Hebrews 11:17-19 and James 2:21-23 both look back to this chapter. What does each writer draw from it about faith?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/binding-of-isaac/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:binding-of-isaac"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Romans 8:32 says God \"didn't spare his own Son\". Reading Genesis 22 alongside it, what do you learn about the cost of God's love?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/binding-of-isaac/check/6",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:binding-of-isaac"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Where in your own life is it hardest to trust that \"Yahweh will provide\", and what helps you keep walking up the mountain?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-ezra/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:book-of-ezra"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Compare Ezra 1:1-4 with 2 Chronicles 36:22-23. What do the two passages share, and what does that suggest about how the story of Israel continues after the exile?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-ezra/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:book-of-ezra"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Ezra 3:10-13, why do some people shout for joy while older priests and Levites weep at the laying of the Temple's foundation?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-ezra/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:book-of-ezra"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What stopped the rebuilding in Ezra 4:24, and according to Ezra 6:14, through whose prophesying did the elders build and prosper?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-ezra/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:book-of-ezra"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Ezra 7:10 says Ezra set his heart to seek the law, to do it and to teach it. Why do you think the order of those three verbs matters for anyone who studies Scripture?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-ezra/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:book-of-ezra"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Ezra's prayer in chapter 9 confesses the sins of the whole community, not just his own. What might it look like for a church to pray that way today?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:book-of-jeremiah"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Jeremiah 1:4-10, what objection does Jeremiah raise to God's call, and what two kinds of work (tearing down and building up) is he given?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:book-of-jeremiah"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Jeremiah 7:1-15, why could the Temple not protect the people of Judah, and what did God want from them instead?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:book-of-jeremiah"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What does Jeremiah 29:4-7 tell the exiles to do in Babylon, and how does verse 11 read differently once you know it was written to people facing seventy years away from home?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:book-of-jeremiah"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Read Jeremiah 31:31-34 alongside Luke 22:20 and Hebrews 8:8-13. What is \"new\" about the new covenant, and how do the New Testament writers see it fulfilled?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:book-of-jeremiah"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Jeremiah 20:7-18 the prophet both praises God and curses the day he was born. What does it mean to you that such honest prayers are part of Scripture?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah/check/6",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:book-of-jeremiah"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Jeremiah buys a field in a city under siege (Jeremiah 32:6-15). Where might God be asking you or your church to act in hope when circumstances look bleak?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/calling-of-the-first-disciples/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:calling-of-the-first-disciples"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Mark 1:14-20, what does Jesus announce just before he calls the four fishermen, and how does that announcement explain why they are called?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/calling-of-the-first-disciples/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:calling-of-the-first-disciples"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What exactly do Simon and Andrew leave in Mark 1:18, and what do James and John leave in Mark 1:20? Why might Mark mention Zebedee and the hired servants?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/calling-of-the-first-disciples/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:calling-of-the-first-disciples"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Luke 5:1-11, what happens between Jesus's request to use Simon's boat and Simon's words \"Depart from me, for I am a sinful man, Lord\"? What changes Simon's mind about who Jesus is?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/calling-of-the-first-disciples/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:calling-of-the-first-disciples"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In John 1:35-42 and 1:45-46, how does each person come to Jesus? What do \"Come, and see\" and \"We have found the Messiah\" suggest about the way faith spreads?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/calling-of-the-first-disciples/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:calling-of-the-first-disciples"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Compare Elisha's call in 1 Kings 19:19-21 with the fishermen's call. What is similar, what is different, and what does that suggest about who Jesus is?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/calling-of-the-first-disciples/check/6",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:calling-of-the-first-disciples"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "The first disciples were ordinary working people called in the middle of their work. What \"nets\" might Jesus be asking you to leave, and what might he be asking you to bring with you?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/catholic-church/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:catholic-church"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In 2 Thessalonians 2:15, by what two means does Paul say the Thessalonians were taught, and how does Catholic teaching draw on that verse?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/catholic-church/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:catholic-church"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to 2 Timothy 3:15-17, what is Scripture able to do for the believer, and what does it equip them for?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/catholic-church/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:catholic-church"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In 1 Corinthians 10:1-11, how does Paul read the crossing of the sea and the wilderness years, and how does that example help explain the \"spiritual senses\" of Scripture?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/catholic-church/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:catholic-church"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Acts 2:42 lists four things the first believers devoted themselves to. Which of them shape how your own church hears the Bible?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/catholic-church/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:catholic-church"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What would help you describe the Catholic way of reading Scripture accurately to a friend from another tradition, or describe another tradition's way accurately to a Catholic friend?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/crucifixion-of-jesus/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:crucifixion-of-jesus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Read Mark 15:16-32. Who mocks Jesus, and what title keeps coming back in their mockery and in the charge fixed to the cross?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/crucifixion-of-jesus/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:crucifixion-of-jesus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In John 19:24 the soldiers divide Jesus's clothes \"that the Scripture might be fulfilled\". Read Psalm 22 to the end. How does knowing the whole psalm change the way you hear Jesus's cry in Mark 15:34?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/crucifixion-of-jesus/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:crucifixion-of-jesus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Compare what the centurion says in Mark 15:39 with Luke 23:47. What does each Gospel want its readers to notice?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/crucifixion-of-jesus/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:crucifixion-of-jesus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Paul calls Christ crucified \"a stumbling block\" and \"foolishness\" (1 Corinthians 1:23). Why might the cross have seemed so, and where does it still cut against what we expect of God?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/crucifixion-of-jesus/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:crucifixion-of-jesus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "The Catholic Church teaches that sinners, not one people, bear the blame for the Passion. How should that shape the way we tell this story in church and at home?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/dead-sea-scrolls/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:dead-sea-scrolls"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Every book of the Hebrew Bible except one is represented among the scrolls. Which book is missing, and why might the absence of a book from a small, damaged collection prove very little?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/dead-sea-scrolls/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:dead-sea-scrolls"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Compare Deuteronomy 32:8 in two English translations. How do they end the verse, and what does the difference tell you about the manuscripts behind them?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/dead-sea-scrolls/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:dead-sea-scrolls"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Both the Qumran community and Mark 1:2-3 used Isaiah 40:3 about the wilderness. How did each understand the \"way\" being prepared?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/dead-sea-scrolls/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:dead-sea-scrolls"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "How does it affect your confidence in Scripture to learn that a scroll copied before Jesus's birth reads almost exactly like the Isaiah in your Bible, while also showing small differences?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/deuteronomy/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:deuteronomy"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Where and when does Moses speak, according to Deuteronomy 1:1-5? Why might it matter that the people are standing on the edge of the land rather than at Sinai?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/deuteronomy/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:deuteronomy"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Deuteronomy 5:2-3 Moses says the covenant at Horeb was made \"with us, even us, who are all of us here alive today\". Most of his listeners were born after Sinai. What is he asking them to understand about God's covenant, and how might that apply to a reader today?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/deuteronomy/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:deuteronomy"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Read the Shema (Deuteronomy 6:4-9). List the places and times of day where God's words are to be kept. What would that look like in your household or small group?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/deuteronomy/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:deuteronomy"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Deuteronomy 30:11-14 says the commandment is \"not too hard\" and \"very near\". How does that sit with the warnings in the rest of the chapter?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/deuteronomy/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:deuteronomy"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "When Jesus is tempted in the wilderness (Matthew 4:1-11), every answer he gives comes from Deuteronomy. Why do you think he reached for this book in particular?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/deuteronomy/check/6",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:deuteronomy"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Moses sees the land but does not enter it (Deuteronomy 34:4-5). What does his story teach about faithfulness when we do not see the end of what God is doing?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/eastern-orthodoxy/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:eastern-orthodoxy"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Luke 24:27 and 24:45, what does the risen Jesus do with \"the Scriptures\", and why do Orthodox Christians treat these verses as the pattern for all Bible reading?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/eastern-orthodoxy/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:eastern-orthodoxy"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "The Ethiopian official in Acts 8:31 asks how he can understand \"unless someone explains it\". Who explains it, and where does Philip begin (Acts 8:35)?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/eastern-orthodoxy/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:eastern-orthodoxy"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What does 2 Peter 1:4 say believers may become, and how does the Orthodox teaching of theosis read that verse?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/eastern-orthodoxy/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:eastern-orthodoxy"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "The Synod of Jerusalem (1672) limited private reading of Scripture, while modern Orthodox teachers urge parish Bible study. What concern lies behind each, and how might they fit together?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/eastern-orthodoxy/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:eastern-orthodoxy"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Which of the Orthodox emphases (Christ as the key, the Fathers, the liturgy, the saints) could deepen your own reading, whatever your tradition?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/elijah/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:elijah"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In 1 Kings 18:21, what choice does Elijah put to the people on Mount Carmel, and how do they answer in verse 39?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/elijah/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:elijah"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What does Elijah say to God in 1 Kings 19:4 and 19:10, and how does God care for him and answer him in 19:5-18?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/elijah/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:elijah"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to 1 Kings 19:11-12, where was the LORD not found, and how did he come to Elijah?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/elijah/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:elijah"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In 1 Kings 21:17-20, why is Elijah sent to Ahab after Naboth's death? What does this show about the God Elijah served?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/elijah/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:elijah"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "How do Malachi 4:5-6, Luke 1:17 and Matthew 17:10-13 connect Elijah with John the Baptist?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/elijah/check/6",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:elijah"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "James 5:17 says Elijah had \"a nature like ours.\" Where have you felt Elijah's exhaustion or loneliness, and what in God's care for him at Horeb speaks to you?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/forgiveness-in-the-bible/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:forgiveness-in-the-bible"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "How does God describe himself to Moses in Exodus 34:6-7, and what does that tell us about where forgiveness begins?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/forgiveness-in-the-bible/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:forgiveness-in-the-bible"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Matthew 18:21-35, how large is the first servant's debt compared with what his fellow servant owes him, and what point is Jesus making by the contrast?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/forgiveness-in-the-bible/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:forgiveness-in-the-bible"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Luke 17:3-4 speaks of rebuking a brother who sins and forgiving him when he repents. How does that fit with Jesus praying for those crucifying him in Luke 23:34?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/forgiveness-in-the-bible/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:forgiveness-in-the-bible"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What did Joseph's forgiveness of his brothers in Genesis 50:15-21 include, and what did it not pretend?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/forgiveness-in-the-bible/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:forgiveness-in-the-bible"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Is there someone I find hard to forgive? What would it look like to begin by praying for them, even before my feelings change?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/galilee/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:galilee"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What happened to Galilee in 2 Kings 15:29, and how does Isaiah 9:1-2 answer that memory of loss?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/galilee/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:galilee"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Matthew 4:12-16, why did Jesus settle in Capernaum, and which prophecy does Matthew see fulfilled there?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/galilee/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:galilee"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Mark 1:14-20, what is the first thing Jesus does in Galilee, and whom does he call beside the lake?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/galilee/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:galilee"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "John 1:46 and John 7:52 show people doubting that anything good could come from Galilee. Why might God have chosen such an unlikely place, and where do you see him working in \"unlikely\" places today?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/galilee/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:galilee"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "After the resurrection, the risen Jesus sends his disciples back to Galilee (Matthew 28:7-10, 16). What might it mean that the mission to \"all nations\" began from the place where they first met him?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:genesis"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Read Genesis 1:26-28 and 1:31. What does God say about human beings, and how does he judge everything he has made?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:genesis"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Genesis 2:4 and 37:2 both begin with \"This is the history of the generations of…\". How does noticing this repeated heading help you see the shape of the whole book?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:genesis"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What three things does God promise Abram in Genesis 12:1-3, and who, finally, is to share in the blessing?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:genesis"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Genesis 50:20 Joseph looks back on his brothers' cruelty. What does he say about their intentions and about God's? Where have you seen God bring good out of something meant for harm?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:genesis"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Paul quotes Genesis 15:6 in Romans 4:3 and Genesis 12:3 in Galatians 3:8. Why do you think the apostle reaches back to Genesis to explain the gospel?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis/check/6",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:genesis"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Genesis opens with a world declared \"very good\" and closes with a family in a foreign land waiting for God's promise. What does that tell you about where the story is heading?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:genre-in-the-bible"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Read Exodus 14:21-31 and then Exodus 15:1-10. What does the song add to the narrative account of the same event?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:genre-in-the-bible"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Psalm 98:8 calls on rivers to clap their hands. What is the psalmist inviting us to see and do?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:genre-in-the-bible"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "How does Luke describe his purpose in Luke 1:1-4, and what does that tell you about the kind of book he is writing?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:genre-in-the-bible"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Revelation 1:1-4 calls the book a revelation, a prophecy and (by its greeting) a letter. How might each of these shape the way you read it?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:genre-in-the-bible"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Which part of the Bible do you find hardest to read, and could knowing more about its kind of writing help?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/example",
   "@type": "bgo:Rewrite",
   "bgo:after": "These are proverbs, not laws. Placed side by side, they teach that sometimes silence is wise and sometimes a reply is needed, and wisdom lies in discerning which situation I am in.",
   "bgo:before": "Verse 4 says don't answer a fool and verse 5 says answer him, so one of these must be wrong, and Proverbs can't be trusted.",
   "bgo:situation": "A small-group member reads Proverbs 26:4 and 26:5 side by side and concludes that the Bible contradicts itself.",
   "bgo:why": "Proverbs are short sayings that capture general truths for particular situations; reading them as rigid rules or guarantees misses how the genre works."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Genre in the Bible",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/6"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Before interpreting a passage, ask what kind of writing it is (narrative, law, poetry, proverb, prophecy, gospel, letter or apocalypse) and look for clues the book gives about itself."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Note the features of that kind of writing, such as parallel lines and imagery in poetry, short general sayings in proverbs, or greetings and arguments in letters."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Ask what that kind of writing is designed to do (tell what happened, command, praise, give practical wisdom, warn, comfort or encourage endurance) and let that purpose guide your conclusions."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Compare passages where the Bible tells the same thing in two forms, such as the Red Sea in Exodus 14 and 15, and notice what each form adds."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Check your genre judgment with a study Bible or Bible dictionary, and hold it humbly where careful readers disagree."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genre-in-the-bible/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Apply the passage in a way that fits its genre, taking a promise as a promise, a proverb as wise counsel and a song as praise to join."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/giving-of-the-law-at-sinai/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:giving-of-the-law-at-sinai"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Exodus 19:4-6, what does God remind Israel he has already done, and what does he say they will become if they keep his covenant?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/giving-of-the-law-at-sinai/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:giving-of-the-law-at-sinai"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Why do the people ask Moses to speak to them instead of God (Exodus 20:18-21; Deuteronomy 5:23-27)? What does Moses say the fear is meant to do?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/giving-of-the-law-at-sinai/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:giving-of-the-law-at-sinai"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What happens with the blood in Exodus 24:6-8, and how do Jesus's words over the cup in Mark 14:24 echo Moses' words?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/giving-of-the-law-at-sinai/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:giving-of-the-law-at-sinai"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Deuteronomy 5:3 tells a later generation that the covenant was made \"with us\". In what sense does a story that happened long ago become your story too?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/giving-of-the-law-at-sinai/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:giving-of-the-law-at-sinai"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Hebrews 12:18-24 contrasts Sinai with Mount Zion. How should both the holiness of Sinai and the welcome of Zion shape the way you come to God in worship?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:gospel-of-luke"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Read Luke 1:1-4. What does Luke say about how he gathered his material, and why does he say he is writing to Theophilus?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:gospel-of-luke"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In the synagogue at Nazareth (Luke 4:16-21) Jesus reads from Isaiah 61. Who is the good news for, and what does he say has happened \"today\"?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:gospel-of-luke"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Luke 15 opens with a complaint that Jesus \"receiveth sinners, and eateth with them\" (15:2). How do the three stories that follow answer it, and why does the last one end with the elder brother still outside?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:gospel-of-luke"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Luke 10:29 the lawyer asks \"who is my neighbor?\", but in 10:36 Jesus asks which man \"proved neighbor\". How does that change of question change the way you read the parable?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:gospel-of-luke"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Luke 24 ends with the risen Jesus opening the Scriptures to his disciples (24:27, 44-45). How might reading the Old Testament \"concerning himself\" shape the way you read it this week?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-mark/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:gospel-of-mark"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Mark calls Jesus \"the Son of God\" in his first verse (1:1). Who else says so, or something like it, at 1:11, 9:7 and 15:39, and why might it matter that the last voice is a Roman centurion at the cross?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-mark/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:gospel-of-mark"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Mark 8:29-31 Peter confesses \"Thou art the Christ,\" and Jesus at once begins to teach that the Son of Man must suffer. Why do you think the two belong together, and what did Peter get wrong?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-mark/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:gospel-of-mark"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Read Mark 10:45. What does it say the Son of Man came to do, and how does it explain the request of James and John just before it (10:35-44)?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-mark/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:gospel-of-mark"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "The oldest manuscripts end at 16:8 with the women saying \"nothing to any one; for they were afraid\" (ASV). What is the young man's message in 16:7, and what might an ending like this ask of the reader?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-mark/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:gospel-of-mark"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Mark shows the disciples misunderstanding, failing and running away, yet Jesus sends word to \"his disciples and Peter\" (16:7). What encouragement does that give to people who follow Jesus imperfectly?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-matthew/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:gospel-of-matthew"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Matthew 1:1 calls Jesus \"the son of David, the son of Abraham.\" Why might Matthew open with those two names in particular?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-matthew/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:gospel-of-matthew"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Find the sentence that closes each of the five teaching blocks (Matthew 7:28, 11:1, 13:53, 19:1 and 26:1). What does each discourse teach disciples about life in the kingdom?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-matthew/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:gospel-of-matthew"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Matthew 5:17-20, what does Jesus say he came to do with the Law and the Prophets, and what kind of righteousness does he ask of his followers?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-matthew/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:gospel-of-matthew"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "The Gospel begins with \"God with us\" (1:23) and ends with \"I am with you always\" (28:20). How does that promise frame everything in between, and where do you need to hear it this week?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospels/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:gospels"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Mark 1:1 calls what follows \"the beginning of the gospel of Jesus Christ\". What does the word \"gospel\" mean, and where in Isaiah 40 and 52 does the idea of a messenger with good news come from?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospels/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:gospels"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Luke 1:1-4, what did Luke know about earlier accounts and eyewitnesses, and why did he write his own?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospels/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:gospels"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "John 20:30-31 says many signs were left out. What does John say his book is for, and how might that purpose shape the way you read any of the Gospels?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospels/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:gospels"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Paul summarises \"the gospel\" in 1 Corinthians 15:1-5. Which of those events do all four Gospels tell at length, and why do you think they give them so much space?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospels/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:gospels"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Choose one story told in more than one Gospel. Read the versions side by side. What does each writer emphasise, and what would be lost if we merged them into one account?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/grace/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:grace"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Exodus 34:6 is God's own description of himself to Moses. Which words in it describe grace, and why is it striking that this comes right after the golden calf?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/grace/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:grace"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Ephesians 2:8-10, what saves us, what does not, and what are we then created for?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/grace/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:grace"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Romans 6:1-2, what wrong conclusion does Paul expect someone to draw from \"grace abounded\", and how does he answer it?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/grace/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:grace"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Paul hears \"My grace is sufficient for you\" in a time of weakness (2 Corinthians 12:9). Where in your own life, or your church's, do you most need grace as strength rather than only as pardon?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/grace/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:grace"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Each Christian tradition says that salvation begins with God's grace. How might that shared conviction change the way you talk with Christians of another tradition?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/hebrew-poetry/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:hebrew-poetry"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Read Psalm 1:1 slowly. What three verbs describe the person's movement, and what does the sequence suggest about how we drift into the company of scoffers?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/hebrew-poetry/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:hebrew-poetry"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Psalm 19:1-2, how does the second line of each verse repeat the first, and what does it add?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/hebrew-poetry/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:hebrew-poetry"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Proverbs 11:1-3 sets up contrasts with \"but\". What two ways of life are being compared, and which one are you invited to choose?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/hebrew-poetry/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:hebrew-poetry"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Psalm 23 pictures God as a shepherd. Which details of the image speak most to you, and what would be lost if the psalm simply said \"God takes care of me\"?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/hebrew-poetry/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:hebrew-poetry"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Psalm 119 and Lamentations 1 are both arranged by the letters of the Hebrew alphabet. Why might a poet use such a pattern for a love of God's law and for grief over a fallen city?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/hebrew-poetry/check/6",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:hebrew-poetry"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "How does Mary's song in Luke 1:46-55 continue the way Israel's psalms pray and praise?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/inductive-bible-study/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:inductive-bible-study"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Acts 17:10-12, what did the Jews of Beroea do with Paul's message, and how often?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/inductive-bible-study/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:inductive-bible-study"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Ezra 7:10 describes Ezra's commitment to God's law in three verbs. What are they, and why might the order matter?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/inductive-bible-study/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:inductive-bible-study"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "James 1:22-25 compares a hearer who does not act to someone looking in a mirror. What point is James making about study and application?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/inductive-bible-study/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:inductive-bible-study"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Read Mark 4:35-41 slowly and list everything you observe before deciding what it means. What did you notice that you had missed before?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/inductive-bible-study/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:inductive-bible-study"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Which of the phases (observation, interpretation, correlation, application) do you tend to skip, and how could your group help you slow down?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/inductive-bible-study/example",
   "@type": "bgo:Rewrite",
   "bgo:after": "The disciples end by asking who Jesus is, since even wind and sea obey him; the passage first shows his identity and calls me to trust him in the storm, whether or not it stops.",
   "bgo:before": "This story promises that Jesus will make the storms in my life go away if I have enough faith.",
   "bgo:situation": "A small group opens Mark 4:35-41, the stilling of the storm, during a hard season for one of its members.",
   "bgo:why": "Observing the closing question (Mark 4:41) and its echo of God calming the sea in Psalm 107:29 moves the group from a quick application to the passage's own focus on who Jesus is."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/inductive-bible-study/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Inductive Bible Study",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/inductive-bible-study/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/inductive-bible-study/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/inductive-bible-study/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/inductive-bible-study/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/inductive-bible-study/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/inductive-bible-study/howto/6"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/inductive-bible-study/howto/7"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/inductive-bible-study/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Pray for understanding, then choose a unit to study (a paragraph, a chapter or a whole short book) and read it through several times without notes or commentary."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/inductive-bible-study/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Observe before you explain - write down who is involved, what happens or is argued, where and when, and note repeated words, contrasts, questions, turning points and the kind of writing it is."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/inductive-bible-study/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Turn your observations into questions (what does this mean, why is it here, why is it said this way?) and answer them first from the passage and its surrounding book."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/inductive-bible-study/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Only after your own study, check your conclusions against a good study Bible, Bible dictionary or commentary, and revise where the evidence points elsewhere."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/inductive-bible-study/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Correlate the passage with the rest of Scripture, asking how other texts on the same subject, and the whole story centred on Christ, shed light on it."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/inductive-bible-study/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Ask what the passage meant for its first readers and what it calls you to believe, pray or do now, and write down one concrete response."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/inductive-bible-study/howto/7",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 7,
   "schema:text": "Share what you found with others, ideally in a small group, so that your reading can be tested and enriched."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/israelites/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:israelites"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Why does Jacob receive the new name \"Israel\" in Genesis 32:28, and what does God promise him when he confirms the name in Genesis 35:9-12?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/israelites/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:israelites"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Deuteronomy 7:6-9, why did God choose Israel, and what was not the reason?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/israelites/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:israelites"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What does God ask of Israel in Exodus 19:5-6, and what does he say Israel will become?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/israelites/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:israelites"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Romans 9:4-5 Paul lists the gifts that belong to the Israelites. Which of these gifts have reached you, and how might that shape the way you speak about the Jewish people?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/israelites/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:israelites"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Israel was not chosen for being large or impressive (Deuteronomy 7:7). How does it change your sense of belonging to God to know that his choice rests on love rather than merit?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/jeremiahs-temple-sermon/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:jeremiahs-temple-sermon"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Where does God tell Jeremiah to stand in Jeremiah 7:2, and who would be passing by as he spoke?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/jeremiahs-temple-sermon/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:jeremiahs-temple-sermon"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What were the people repeating in Jeremiah 7:4 and 7:10, and why did those words feel like a guarantee of safety?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/jeremiahs-temple-sermon/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:jeremiahs-temple-sermon"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Which wrongs does Jeremiah list in 7:5-9? How do they line up with the Ten Commandments and with care for the foreigner, the fatherless and the widow?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/jeremiahs-temple-sermon/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:jeremiahs-temple-sermon"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Why does God send the listeners to look at Shiloh (7:12-14)? What had happened there?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/jeremiahs-temple-sermon/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:jeremiahs-temple-sermon"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Jeremiah 26 the elders remember Micah's words about Zion (26:18-19). How does that memory save Jeremiah's life, and what does it suggest about how God's warnings work?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/jeremiahs-temple-sermon/check/6",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:jeremiahs-temple-sermon"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Jesus quotes Jeremiah 7:11 in the Temple (Mark 11:17). What does the original sermon add to your understanding of that scene?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/jeremiahs-temple-sermon/check/7",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:jeremiahs-temple-sermon"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What \"safe words\" or religious habits might a church or a believer lean on today instead of a changed life, and how could this passage gently correct that?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/jerusalem/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:jerusalem"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to 2 Samuel 5:6-9, who lived in Jerusalem before David, and what did David call the stronghold once he took it?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/jerusalem/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:jerusalem"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Read Psalm 122. Why were pilgrims glad to go up to Jerusalem, and what does the psalmist ask readers to pray for?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/jerusalem/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:jerusalem"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Isaiah 2:2-4, who comes to Jerusalem in the \"latter days\", and what do they go away with?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/jerusalem/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:jerusalem"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Luke 9:51 says Jesus \"intently set his face\" to go to Jerusalem, and Luke 19:41-44 shows him weeping over it. What do these two moments tell you about how Jesus regarded the city?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/jerusalem/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:jerusalem"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Revelation 21 describes a New Jerusalem with no temple in it. What does that suggest about where God means to live, and how might that hope shape the way you worship now?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/jesus/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:jesus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Matthew 1:21, why is the child to be named Jesus? What does that tell you about what he came to do?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/jesus/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:jesus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What does Jesus announce when he begins preaching in Mark 1:14-15, and what does he ask his hearers to do?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/jesus/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:jesus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Matthew 16:13-16, Jesus asks \"But who do you say that I am?\" How does Peter answer, and how would you answer in your own words?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/jesus/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:jesus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Luke 24:27 and 24:44, which parts of the Scriptures does Jesus say speak about him? Which Old Testament passage you know might point to him, and how?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/jesus/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:jesus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Philippians 2:5-11 begins \"Have this in your mind.\" What attitude of Jesus does Paul want his readers to share, and where could you practise it this week?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/john-the-baptist/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:john-the-baptist"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Luke 1:13-17, what did the angel tell Zechariah his son would be and do, and whose \"spirit and power\" would he go in?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/john-the-baptist/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:john-the-baptist"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What did John tell the crowds, the tax collectors and the soldiers to do in Luke 3:10-14? What do his answers show about the repentance he preached?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/john-the-baptist/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:john-the-baptist"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In John 1:19-23 John says who he is not before he says who he is. What does he call himself, and which prophet is he quoting?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/john-the-baptist/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:john-the-baptist"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Why might John, in prison, have sent to ask Jesus, \"Are you he who comes?\" (Matthew 11:3), and how does Jesus answer from Isaiah's promises rather than with a plain yes?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/john-the-baptist/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:john-the-baptist"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "\"He must increase, but I must decrease\" (John 3:30). Where in your church life or service is it hardest to point away from yourself to Christ?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/kingdom-of-god/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:kingdom-of-god"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Mark 1:14-15, what does Jesus announce when he begins preaching in Galilee, and what two responses does he ask for?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/kingdom-of-god/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:kingdom-of-god"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Luke 11:20, what does Jesus point to as a sign that God's Kingdom \"has come to you\"?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/kingdom-of-god/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:kingdom-of-god"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What do the parables of the seed growing by itself and the mustard seed (Mark 4:26-32) suggest about how God's Kingdom grows, and who makes it grow?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/kingdom-of-god/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:kingdom-of-god"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Psalm 145:13 calls God's Kingdom everlasting, yet Jesus teaches us to pray \"Let your Kingdom come\" (Matthew 6:10). How can both be true?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/kingdom-of-god/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:kingdom-of-god"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "When you pray the Lord's Prayer, where in your own life, family or church do you most long to see God's will done \"as in heaven, so on earth\"?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/laying-the-foundation-of-the-second-temple/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:laying-the-foundation-of-the-second-temple"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Ezra 3:2-6, what did the returned exiles build first, and what did they begin doing even though the Temple's foundation \"was not yet laid\"?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/laying-the-foundation-of-the-second-temple/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:laying-the-foundation-of-the-second-temple"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Ezra 3:3 says the people built the altar while \"fear was on them\". What does it suggest that they worshipped anyway?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/laying-the-foundation-of-the-second-temple/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:laying-the-foundation-of-the-second-temple"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What did the priests and Levites sing when the foundation was laid (Ezra 3:11), and where else in Scripture does that refrain appear?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/laying-the-foundation-of-the-second-temple/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:laying-the-foundation-of-the-second-temple"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Why did the older priests and Levites weep in Ezra 3:12? How does Haggai 2:3-9 speak to the same feeling?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/laying-the-foundation-of-the-second-temple/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:laying-the-foundation-of-the-second-temple"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Have you known a moment, in your own life or your church's, when joy and grief were mixed together so that you \"could not discern\" one from the other? What does this passage give you to bring to such a moment?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:lectio-divina"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Psalm 1:1-3, where does the blessed person find delight, and what picture describes the result of meditating day and night?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:lectio-divina"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Joshua 1:8 says the book of the law should not depart from Joshua's mouth. What does that suggest about how meditation was practised, and what is it meant to lead to?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:lectio-divina"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What did Mary do with the shepherds' words in Luke 2:19, and how is that like the step of meditatio?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:lectio-divina"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Luke 10:38-42, what is Mary doing, what is Martha doing, and why does Jesus defend Mary?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:lectio-divina"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Which movement (reading, meditation, prayer, contemplation or action) comes hardest for you, and how could a small group help you grow in it?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/example",
   "@type": "bgo:Rewrite",
   "bgo:after": "In the scene, Jesus defends Mary for sitting and listening to him while Martha is pulled apart by her serving; he invites me to put listening to him first and to notice where worry crowds it out, and my serving can grow from that.",
   "bgo:before": "Jesus' words to Martha about the one thing needed jumped out at me, so God is telling me to quit the hospitality team.",
   "bgo:situation": "A member of a small group prays through Luke 10:38-42, the visit of Jesus to Martha and Mary, during a busy season of church volunteering.",
   "bgo:why": "Lectio begins by asking what the text says in itself before asking what it says to me, so a striking phrase is heard within its scene instead of as a free-floating private message."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Lectio Divina",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/6"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Choose a short passage of a few verses, such as a Gospel scene or a psalm, settle into quiet, and ask God to speak to you through his word."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Lectio - read the passage slowly several times, aloud if you can, and first ask what the text says in itself and where it sits in its chapter."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Meditatio - stay with a word or phrase that stands out, turn it over, and ask what that meaning says to your life today."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Oratio - answer God in your own words, with thanks, confession, questions or requests drawn from the passage."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Contemplatio - rest quietly before God for a few minutes without trying to produce more thoughts."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Actio - choose one concrete way to live out what you received, and test any strong impression against the wider Bible and with your church or small group."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:lords-prayer"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Compare Matthew 6:9-13 with Luke 11:2-4. Which petitions do both share, and what setting does each Gospel give the prayer (Matthew 6:5-8; Luke 11:1)?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:lords-prayer"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "The first petitions are about God's name, kingdom and will; the later ones about our bread, our sins and our testing. What does that order teach about how to pray?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:lords-prayer"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Every pronoun in the prayer is plural (\"our\", \"us\"). How does praying it change if I picture my church, or the believers I find hardest to love, praying it with me?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:lords-prayer"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Matthew 6:14-15 Jesus adds a comment on just one petition. Which one, and why might he single it out?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:lords-prayer"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Jesus prays \"your desire be done\" in Gethsemane (Matthew 26:42). How does that scene deepen what it means to pray \"your will be done\"?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/loving-your-neighbor/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:loving-your-neighbor"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Read Leviticus 19:9-18. Which concrete actions does the chapter list before it reaches \"love your neighbor as yourself,\" and what do they show about what love means there?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/loving-your-neighbor/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:loving-your-neighbor"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Luke 10:29 the lawyer asks \"Who is my neighbor?\" How does Jesus's question in Luke 10:36 turn that question around?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/loving-your-neighbor/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:loving-your-neighbor"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Romans 13:8-10 and Galatians 5:14, how is love of neighbor related to the rest of God's commandments?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/loving-your-neighbor/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:loving-your-neighbor"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What does 1 John 4:20-21 say about someone who claims to love God but hates a brother or sister?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/loving-your-neighbor/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:loving-your-neighbor"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Who is a \"neighbor\" I find easy to pass by, at church, at work or on my street, and what is one act of mercy I could offer this week?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/masoretic-text/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:masoretic-text"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Read Psalm 100:3 in the King James Version and in the World English Bible. How do they differ, and how does the Masoretic note about what is \"written\" and what is \"read\" explain it?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/masoretic-text/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:masoretic-text"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Nehemiah 8:8 the Levites read the law \"distinctly\" and \"gave the sense\". How did the Masoretes' vowel signs and accents serve the same goal?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/masoretic-text/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:masoretic-text"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Luke 4:16-17, what was Jesus handed in the synagogue at Nazareth, and what does that tell you about how Scripture was read in his day?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/masoretic-text/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:masoretic-text"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Why might the Masoretes have counted the verses, words and even letters of Scripture? What does that care suggest about how they regarded the text?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/masoretic-text/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:masoretic-text"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "How does it shape your trust in the Old Testament to know that much of it reached your Bible through generations of Jewish scribes?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/money-and-generosity/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:money-and-generosity"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Deuteronomy 15:7-11, what attitude of heart does God forbid toward a poor neighbor, and what does he command instead?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/money-and-generosity/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:money-and-generosity"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Luke 12:13-21, what prompts Jesus to tell the parable of the rich fool, and what does it mean to be \"rich toward God\" (Luke 12:21)?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/money-and-generosity/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:money-and-generosity"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Why does Jesus say in Mark 12:43-44 that the widow gave more than all the rich donors?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/money-and-generosity/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:money-and-generosity"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Read 1 Timothy 6:10 carefully. Does it say that money is the root of all evil? What exactly does it warn against?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/money-and-generosity/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:money-and-generosity"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Paul grounds giving in the grace of Christ, who became poor for our sake (2 Corinthians 8:9). How might that change the way I or my church think about giving?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/money-and-generosity/check/6",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:money-and-generosity"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Where is my \"treasure\" (Matthew 6:21) at present, and what is one concrete step toward open-handed generosity I could take this month?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/mosaic-covenant/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:mosaic-covenant"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Deuteronomy 7:7-8, why did the Lord choose Israel and bring them out of Egypt? What does that order (love first, commandments after) tell you about the covenant?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/mosaic-covenant/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:mosaic-covenant"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What is the sign of this covenant in Exodus 31:13-17, and what two things does keeping it remind Israel of?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/mosaic-covenant/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:mosaic-covenant"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Leviticus 26 and Deuteronomy 28-30 set out blessings and curses. What does God promise in Leviticus 26:44-45 and Deuteronomy 30:6 even after the covenant has been broken?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/mosaic-covenant/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:mosaic-covenant"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Deuteronomy 29:14-15 Moses says the covenant is made also with those \"not here with us this day\". How do Joshua 24 and 2 Kings 23 show later generations taking it up as their own?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/mosaic-covenant/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:mosaic-covenant"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Jeremiah 31:32-33 says the new covenant will be \"not according to\" the one made at the Exodus. What exactly is new, and what stays the same? How does that shape the way you read the laws of Exodus and Leviticus?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:moses"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Exodus 3:7-12, what has God seen and heard, what will he do, and how does he answer Moses' question \"Who am I\"?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:moses"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What excuse does Moses give in Exodus 4:10, and how does God respond in verses 11-17?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:moses"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Exodus 32:11-14 and 32:30-32, what reasons does Moses give God for sparing the people? What does his prayer show about the kind of leader he was?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:moses"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Why was Moses not allowed to lead Israel into the land (Numbers 20:7-12)? What exactly had God told him to do, and what did he do instead?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:moses"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Hebrews 3:5-6 calls Moses a faithful servant in God's house and Christ a faithful Son over it. How does that comparison honour Moses rather than dismiss him?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses/check/6",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:moses"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Moses argued with God, failed, interceded and kept going for forty years. Where in your own calling do you most identify with his reluctance — or with his perseverance?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/new-testament/check/1",
