   "rdfs:label": "Read 2 Samuel 12:1-7. How does Nathan's story get past David's defences, and what happens when David judges the rich man?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/parables-of-jesus/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:parables-of-jesus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Compare the vineyard in Isaiah 5:1-7 with the vineyard in Mark 12:1-12. What would Jesus's hearers have recognised, and why did they realise the parable was \"against them\" (Mark 12:12)?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/parables-of-jesus/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:parables-of-jesus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Luke 15:1-3 tells us who was listening when Jesus told the parables of the lost. How does that audience change the way you read the elder brother?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/parables-of-jesus/check/6",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:parables-of-jesus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Which parable has most unsettled you, and what was it asking you to decide?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/paul-at-the-areopagus/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:paul-at-the-areopagus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What did Paul see in Athens that \"stirred\" his spirit (Acts 17:16), and where did he go to talk with people (17:17)?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/paul-at-the-areopagus/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:paul-at-the-areopagus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Why did some listeners think Paul was proclaiming \"strange gods\" (17:18)? What two things had he been preaching?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/paul-at-the-areopagus/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:paul-at-the-areopagus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Paul quotes a Greek poet in Acts 17:28. What point does he draw from the line in the next verse (17:29)?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/paul-at-the-areopagus/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:paul-at-the-areopagus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "The speech begins with creation and ends with repentance, judgment and the resurrection (17:30-31). Why do you think Paul builds toward Jesus in that order for this audience?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/paul-at-the-areopagus/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:paul-at-the-areopagus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Luke records three responses in 17:32-34. Which response do you see most often when you talk about faith with friends or colleagues, and what might Paul's example teach you about those conversations?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/paul/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:paul"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Acts 9:1-6, what is Saul doing when Jesus meets him, and what question does Jesus ask him?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/paul/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:paul"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Compare Acts 9:20-30 with Galatians 1:15-24. What does each account emphasise about what Paul did after his conversion?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/paul/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:paul"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Philippians 3:4-8, which credentials does Paul list, and how does he now value them?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/paul/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:paul"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Paul calls himself \"the least of the apostles\" yet says God's grace was not in vain (1 Corinthians 15:9-10). How might his story shape the way we see people who have done harm, or our own past?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/pentecost/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:pentecost"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Acts 2:5-11, who makes up the crowd in Jerusalem, and what do they hear the disciples speaking about?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/pentecost/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:pentecost"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "How does Peter explain what is happening in Acts 2:16-21, and which kinds of people does Joel's promise name?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/pentecost/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:pentecost"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Acts 2:37-41, what does Peter tell his hearers to do, and to whom does he say the promise belongs?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/pentecost/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:pentecost"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Leviticus 23 and Deuteronomy 16 make the Feast of Weeks a harvest festival shared with servants, foreigners, orphans and widows. How might that background shape the way you read Acts 2:42-47?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/pentecost/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:pentecost"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "At Babel people stopped understanding one another; at Pentecost each heard God's works in their own language. Where does your church need the Spirit's gift of understanding across differences?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/peter/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:peter"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Matthew 16:13-20, what does Peter confess about Jesus, and where does Jesus say that insight came from?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/peter/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:peter"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Why does Jesus rebuke Peter so sharply in Matthew 16:21-23, only moments after blessing him?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/peter/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:peter"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Compare Jesus' warning in Luke 22:31-34 with his three questions in John 21:15-17. How does the second scene answer the first?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/peter/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:peter"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What did Peter learn at Joppa and in Cornelius's house (Acts 10:28, 10:34-35), and how did he use that lesson at Jerusalem (Acts 15:7-11)?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/peter/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:peter"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Peter failed publicly and was restored and given work to do. Where do you, or your church, need to hear that a failure is not the end of someone's discipleship?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/pharisees/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:pharisees"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Acts 23:6-8, which beliefs did the Pharisees hold that the Sadducees rejected?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/pharisees/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:pharisees"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Matthew 23:2-3, what does Jesus tell the crowds to do with the Pharisees' teaching, and what does he warn them not to copy?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/pharisees/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:pharisees"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Nicodemus (John 3:1-2) and Gamaliel (Acts 5:34-39) were both Pharisees. How do their stories complicate the picture of the Pharisees as simply Jesus's enemies?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/pharisees/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:pharisees"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Jesus's sharpest warnings were aimed at devout, Bible-loving people. Where might Matthew 23:23-28 speak to our own church life today?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/psalm-22/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:psalm-22"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Psalm 22:1-2 the psalmist says God does not answer. Whom is he still speaking to, and what does it mean that he calls God \"my God\"?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/psalm-22/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:psalm-22"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What does the psalmist remember in verses 4-5 and 9-10? How do those memories help him keep praying?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/psalm-22/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:psalm-22"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Find the point where the psalm turns from plea to praise. How far does the praise reach by verses 27-31?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/psalm-22/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:psalm-22"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Compare Psalm 22:7-8 and 22:18 with Matthew 27:35, 39 and 43 and John 19:23-24. What do the Gospel writers want readers to notice?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/psalm-22/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:psalm-22"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Jesus prays the first line of this psalm from the cross (Mark 15:34). How does knowing the whole psalm shape the way you hear his cry?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/psalm-22/check/6",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:psalm-22"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Is there a time when you felt God was far away? What would it look like to pray that honestly, as this psalm does?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/public-ministry-of-jesus/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:public-ministry-of-jesus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Luke 3:1-2 dates John the Baptist's preaching by naming an emperor, a governor, three tetrarchs and two high priests. Why might Luke anchor the story so carefully in public history?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/public-ministry-of-jesus/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:public-ministry-of-jesus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Mark 1:14-15, when and where does Jesus begin preaching, and what are the four parts of his first message?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/public-ministry-of-jesus/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:public-ministry-of-jesus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Luke 4:16-21, what passage does Jesus read in the Nazareth synagogue, and what does he claim about it? What does that suggest about the purpose of his whole ministry?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/public-ministry-of-jesus/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:public-ministry-of-jesus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "How does Mark 8:27-31 change the direction of the story? What does Jesus begin to teach \"from that time\" onward?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/public-ministry-of-jesus/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:public-ministry-of-jesus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Count the Passovers John mentions (John 2:13, 6:4, 11:55). Why do you think the other Gospels never tell us how long the ministry lasted?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/public-ministry-of-jesus/check/6",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:public-ministry-of-jesus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Peter summed up Jesus's ministry as \"doing good and healing\" (Acts 10:38). If someone summed up your church's life in one sentence, what would you hope they said?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/rabbinic-judaism/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:rabbinic-judaism"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Nehemiah 8:1-8, what do Ezra and the Levites do besides reading the law aloud, and why might that matter for the later Jewish practice of interpreting Torah?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/rabbinic-judaism/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:rabbinic-judaism"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Mark 7:1-13, what exactly does Jesus criticise about the \"tradition of the elders\" — the existence of tradition, or tradition that sets aside God's command?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/rabbinic-judaism/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:rabbinic-judaism"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Jesus quotes Hosea 6:6 in Matthew 9:13, and the rabbinic sage Yohanan ben Zakkai is remembered as using the same verse after the Temple fell. What do the two uses have in common?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/rabbinic-judaism/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:rabbinic-judaism"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Paul says in Romans 11:28-29 that God's gifts and calling are irrevocable. How should that shape the way Christians speak about Jewish neighbours and their reading of Scripture?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:reading-in-context"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Jeremiah 29:1-10, who first received the letter containing verse 11, where were they, and how long did God say they would wait?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:reading-in-context"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Read Philippians 4:10-14. What \"all things\" is Paul talking about in verse 13, and how does that change the way the verse is often used?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:reading-in-context"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Revelation 3:20 is often used in evangelism. To whom is it first addressed (Revelation 3:14-22), and what does that add to its meaning?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:reading-in-context"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Which verse do you hold dear but have never read in its surrounding chapter, and what do you notice when you read the whole chapter this week?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/example",
   "@type": "bgo:Rewrite",
   "bgo:after": "God told exiles in Babylon to settle in and seek the city's peace, promising a future after seventy years; I can trust his good purposes and be faithful where I am, even if this interview fails.",
   "bgo:before": "God has promised me success and no setbacks, so this interview is bound to work out.",
   "bgo:situation": "A friend facing a job interview posts Jeremiah 29:11 as a guarantee that everything will go well.",
   "bgo:why": "Reading the whole letter (Jeremiah 29:1-14) shows a promise of long-range hope to a community in exile, which still comforts believers today but not as a pledge of quick personal success."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Reading in Context",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/6"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/7"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Read the whole paragraph, and then the whole chapter, around the verse before deciding what it means."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Ask who is speaking, to whom, and in what situation; note what the book itself tells you about its author and first readers."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Trace the flow of thought by asking what comes just before, what comes just after, and how the verse fits the argument or story."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Identify the kind of writing (letter, poem, prophecy, narrative) and read it the way that kind of writing is meant to be read."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Use a study Bible or Bible dictionary to fill in historical and cultural background, without letting the background drown out the text."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Compare the passage with other Scripture on the same subject, especially clearer passages, and see how it fits the whole story that centres on Christ."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/7",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 7,
   "schema:text": "Only then ask what the passage means for you or your church, applying it in a way its first readers would recognise as faithful to it."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/sadducees-question-about-the-resurrection/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:sadducees-question-about-the-resurrection"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Which law of Moses do the Sadducees build their question on (compare Mark 12:19 with Deuteronomy 25:5-6), and what was that law meant to protect?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/sadducees-question-about-the-resurrection/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:sadducees-question-about-the-resurrection"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Jesus says the Sadducees know neither \"the Scriptures nor the power of God\" (Mark 12:24). Which part of his answer addresses each of those two mistakes?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/sadducees-question-about-the-resurrection/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:sadducees-question-about-the-resurrection"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Read Exodus 3:6 and Mark 12:26-27 side by side. Why does God's naming himself \"the God of Abraham, the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob\" matter for whether the dead will be raised?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/sadducees-question-about-the-resurrection/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:sadducees-question-about-the-resurrection"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Luke adds that \"all are alive to him\" (Luke 20:38). How might that line shape the way a Christian thinks about believers who have died?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/sadducees-question-about-the-resurrection/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:sadducees-question-about-the-resurrection"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Does Jesus say that the risen become angels, or that they are like angels? Why does the difference matter?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/sadducees/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:sadducees"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Mark 12:18-27, what question do the Sadducees put to Jesus, and which passage of the Law of Moses does he answer them from?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/sadducees/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:sadducees"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Acts 23:8, what three things did the Sadducees deny, and how does Paul use that disagreement in Acts 23:6-10?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/sadducees/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:sadducees"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Why were the priests and the Sadducees \"upset\" with Peter and John in Acts 4:1-2?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/sadducees/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:sadducees"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Jesus tells the Sadducees they know neither \"the Scriptures nor the power of God\" (Mark 12:24). How might sincere Bible readers today make a similar mistake, and what helps guard against it?"
  },
